  "guarantees": [
    "Complete immutable ancestor A is proven contained in actual local-origin archive B before constructing the physical wrapper. A and B separately retained in C are insufficient.",
    "Native file closures, physical manifest lineage, exact closed/readiness/unpublished bytes, the formerly active WAL prefix and every original raster file remain required. Equal logical clocks and byte-valid active forks are not containment.",
    "Original prepared-host and cold operational origin fields remain B. New closed revision-one metadata separately retains ancestor, localOrigin, current complete server and every current native participant source.",
    "Actual native/raster custody, complete A/C retention, current capture and protected-stream verification run on blocking native workers under serialized room-then-raster locks. No new router, role, writer, event, provider write, cleanup, acknowledgement or activation.",
    "Every current document/review protected record, including revoked and permanent observers, remains required. Missing credentials yield Pending only after actual source checks; checksum-valid omissions refuse.",
    "Weak nonserializable proof binds exact native host/owner and A/B/C cut. It cannot be constructed by Default or Deserialize, keeps no stopped host alive and is not an activation reservation.",
    "Physical-only rotations, raster-only additions and new registrations stale old proofs. Different actual host or ancestor selections cannot reuse a proof even with equal current bytes.",
    "One authenticated complete server asset-reference read retains exact A/B/C and whole native Ready/Pending under the existing encoded-result bound.",
    "Forty independent grammar/transport/document/review native scenarios and ten public-only Rust profiles keep old offline work and future native Undo/Redo. Separate native laws cover forks, reversal, lost/changed stages/files and altered actual control custody without repair."
  ],
